cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "Information Job Shop (IJS): From Von Neumann Computing to Information Manufacturing"

message: >
  If you use this repository in your research,
  please cite it using the metadata below.

type: report

authors:
  - family-names: Tan
    given-names: Sizhe

abstract: >
  Information Job Shop (IJS) proposes a new engineering paradigm
  in which information itself becomes the computational workpiece.
  Extending the classical Job Shop concept from manufacturing engineering,
  the framework organizes heterogeneous computational resources around
  dynamically evolving Information Jobs and introduces Information
  Manufacturing as a higher-level abstraction for future AI systems.

keywords:
  - Artificial Intelligence
  - Information Job Shop
  - Information Manufacturing
  - Information Jobs
  - AI Agents
  - Large Language Models
  - Human-AI Collaboration
  - Brain Units
  - Runtime Systems
  - Job Shop Scheduling
  - Computational Organization
  - Structural Intelligence

